`results/struct-lb-factcheck-extend.md` §3, claim 6 (organize-archive b5cb45e). The table
reproduces `scripts/struct-lb-e-k2line.out` (b5cb45e): 844 admissible directions `(c, a)` with
`c² + a² ≤ 900`, each covering on segments of length at least `1/696`.

The witnesses were chosen by a greedy cover over the exact cells of each line, among the cells of
length at least the line's own bound. Only the recorded segments enter the proof. Each is checked
in integer arithmetic by `lineWitOK`: the eight gap forms of its context are nonnegative at both
ends and positive at one.

